WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.680
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute&nbsp;
Papers with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:09.600
Today you are going to see virtual&nbsp;
worlds like you’ve never seen before!

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:16.740
This is done with something that we call&nbsp;
NERFs. So, what are NERFs? Essentially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:24.660
we grab a smartphone and a set of images go in,&nbsp;
and reality comes out. When there is a gap between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:31.920
the images, it can synthesize all this information&nbsp;
and it almost looks like reality. Absolute magic.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:38.880
Now, many of these are neural network-based&nbsp;
techniques and take quite a while to compute.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:45.900
However, later NVIDIA published a technique&nbsp;
by the name instant NERFs. As the name says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:52.140
this trains incredibly quickly and is one of&nbsp;
the best techniques in its class. And today,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:58.260
these can be produced from a smartphone camera,&nbsp;
and can be generated in a matter of seconds.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:05.040
But, there is a problem. Do you see the&nbsp;
problem? Well, let me ask you another&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:11.640
question - how do you spot a Fellow Scholar&nbsp;
who watches Two Minute Papers? Well, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:20.220
they are always looking at thin structures. Why?&nbsp;
Well, look! So, instant NERFs are super fast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:26.820
but have trouble with thin structures. And&nbsp;
now, hold on to your papers Fellow Scholars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:35.400
and let’s look at how this new paper deals with&nbsp;
the same problem. Oh my, that is outstanding!

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.700
But wait, it is only better on thin structures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.680
or is it generally better than this&nbsp;
previous technique? Well, let’s see. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:49.500
thin structures are still present, but the&nbsp;
new one is significantly better in terms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:57.480
of quality. Wow. And this is just one year and&nbsp;
one more paper down the line. Very impressive.

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:05.820
Also, here is a comparison against Mip-NERF, this&nbsp;
is real good, so I bet the new one isn’t better,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:12.360
especially that this previous one ran&nbsp;
for about 20 times longer. Let’s see.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:23.520
Is that really possible? The new one&nbsp;
is still better. 20 times faster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:29.400
and we don’t even have to pay for it by&nbsp;
giving up quality. This is still better.

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:36.840
With this, we can now just grab a smartphone&nbsp;
and scan a real place and make a virtual&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:42.900
world out of it. This can be used for a video&nbsp;
games, videoconferencing, animation movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:50.340
you name it. Now, not even this work is perfect,&nbsp;
you see, specular reflections like this display&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:57.780
are not that faithful to reality, and if we look&nbsp;
at severely undersampled regions, this can happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:04.080
However, just think about the fact that all&nbsp;
this came just one more paper down the line.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:09.720
Now combine this together with this amazing&nbsp;
light transport paper that can take photos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:16.320
of real-world objects and create a super&nbsp;
advanced, digital material model with just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:23.640
the right physical parameters to replicate it.&nbsp;
So, NERFs can help with the geometry, and light&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:29.880
transport can help with the materials. And a&nbsp;
potential combination of the two could create&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:37.260
even more incredible virtual worlds and games for&nbsp;
us in the near future. What a time to be alive!

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:26.940
Thanks for watching and for your generous&nbsp;
support, and I'll see you next time!

